      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T05:32:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your observation is correct. When CONFIG_PS2 is defined, the ATL entry for GPIO37 (and also GPIO34) are defined as PS2 function. In gpio.inc of Primus, I see GPIO34 is selected to ALT function (ADC). Unfortunately, when CONFIG_PS2 is defined, it is eventually selected to PS/2 and it will also influence GPIO37 as they share the same configuration bit.\nTo fix it, I perfer to remove the ALT entry for PS2-2 (ans also PS2-3)  in the gpio_chip-npcx9.h. However, it will restrict the hardware circuit implementation (i.e. only PS2-0 and PS2-1 can connect to AUX device).\n\n@caveh What do you think about my suggestion above? I looks like only PS2-0 (on Morphius) and PS2-1(Primus) are used in whole EC boards.",
      "parentUuid": "4d1ebf2a_54cf42e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "aa13ea6e1cfb27d127dfd59286e0e82c2d1d1e4d",
