      "writtenOn": "2021-07-27T06:22:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "wow, i\u0027m glad i looped you in. i didn\u0027t realize these two pins shared\na single ALT control bit for PS2.\n\nso ya, maybe CONFIG_PS2 should be enhanced to allow controlling PS2 ports\nindividually so pins that are not used for PS2 in a design are not forced into PS2 mode.\n\nlooks like PS2_CL2/DAT2 and PS2_CL3 would be affected. can we add a\nconfig option to enable PS2-2 and PS3-3 explicitly? since no board\nappears to be using PS2-2 or PS2-3, just default to disabled.\nif some design ends up needing PS2-2 or PS2-3, they can explicitly\nenable the config for that port.\n\nit\u0027s probably OK to add the config to chip/npcx/config_chip*.h.\nthis is obscure enough that it does not need to be in\ninclude/config.h:\n\n#undef NPCX_PS2_MODULE_2\n#undef NPCX_PS2_MODULE_3\n\nfeel free to suggest a better name 😊",
